style neo ukyo is being judged by  anime standards but we need to get this  straight  right off the bat neo yo Kyo is not an  anime it is a Western cartoon that pays  homage to anime and for those of you who  are not French weaves like me it pays  homage to anime there are definitely a  ton of animate ropes and cliches that  fans of anime will recognize in the  oh-yo kyo random skirt shots  hikiko mori idol culture demon girls  mecca's and so on nevertheless while  paying tribute to anime at its core neo  yo Kyo is far more similar to Western  adult cartoons like Bojack horseman and  Archer vent to anime and this is why we  need to remember that what makes anime  anime is not just an art style the  unique cultural and historical context  also plays a key role and for this  reason avatar is not an anime and  neither is neo yo kyo that said there  are numerous blatant references to anime  in new yoyo kyo including the exorcist /  demon slayer / supernatural detective  genre in anime science fiction themes  inspired by anime like akira teen  romance themes and settings similar to  mole rod host club and Nagi ah su and  there are even direct and or indirect  references to works of sci-fi authors  like William Gibson and philip k dick oh  and is that a [ __ ] Hamlet  reference Neo yo kyo is at its core a  beautiful mess that combines some of the  craziest aspects of anime with some of  the most outrageous elements of Western  culture and to put it simply neo yo kyo  is what happens when all Ron host club  meets daily lives of high-school boys  meets Bojack horseman meets big Tobler  olds the first thing we need to  understand when watching neo yo Kyo is  the type of humor it intentionally  embraces Neil yo Kyo embraces a surreal  or absurdist comedy style which to quote  Wikipedia  is a form of humor predicated on  deliberate violations of causal  reasoning producing events and behaviors  that are obviously illogical the humor  derived gets its appeal from the fact  that the situation described is so  ridiculous or unlikely the whole point  of such humor is to be unrealistic  absurd and over-the-top in order to  shine a spotlight on the absurdity of  the real world by exaggerating to the  point of absurdity it subverts our  expectations and forces us to think  about the actual absurdity in the real  world in our own world in neo yo kyo in  particular the main themes covered are  the general malaise and meaninglessness  of modern urban life along with the  absurd elitism vanity luxury and social  inequality of modern society however as  I said earlier these themes are explored  through exaggerated and absurd  situations which are not meant to be  realistic they are meant to be so  outrageous that they make us stop and  think wait modern society could not  possibly be anything like this could it  good example of similar absurdist  surreal and satirical cartoons are as  mentioned earlier Bojack horseman and  Archer but also the early seasons of  FAMILY GUY films like Napoleon Dynamite  and Borat and of course Adult Swim shows  like Harvey Birdman attorney at law this  type of comedy is not for everyone  many find it to be too outlandish to  relate to but Neil yoki Oh actually fits  really well within this sub-genre going  into neo yo kyo and expecting a serious  attempt to make a sophisticated anime  series is like going into Keijo  expecting a serious sports anime or  going into one punch man and expecting a  Dark Knight esque  gritty superhero story we have to take  neo yo Kyo for what it is and for what  it is it's brilliant  the animation is not great by any means  the music is all over the place and the  show cannot compare to the kind of  quality we have become accustomed to  with most anime but I genuinely enjoyed  neo yo Kyo and I thought it was  hilarious I noticed that a lot of  critics seem to think that neo yo Kyo  takes itself seriously but fails as a  serious show but I do not think that neo  yo Kyo takes itself seriously for a  second for instance I firmly believe  that the melodramatic classical music  interspersed with sudden bursts of jazz  and other genres was not intended to  make the show seem more serious but just  the opposite it is a satire of melodrama  and the fact that inside neo yo Kyo  there is an underground club that plays  grigory and house music says at all in  my mind the absurd situations and  characters the endless parade of anime  tropes and references the protagonists  over-the-top vanity and melodramatic  brooding over pointless [ __ ] and of  course the epic rival Arcangelo I loved  at all Arcangelo is such a cliche overly  competitive douchebag rival character  that it's actually hilarious and in fact  if I'm being honest I prefer him to many  of the rival characters we've seen in  recent popular anime Arcangelo is a  self-obsessed pretentious douchebag to  the core but at least he's open and  honest about it  and at least he does it in style and  this random surreal outlandish humor is  enough for me to enjoy the show on its  own but you can also dig deeper into the  symbolism and meaning behind the show if  you really want to for instance I've  seen a lot of criticism directed at the  main character cast conned  because he is vain shallow melancholic  and doesn't really undergo any  meaningful development throughout the  series but that's exactly the point he  is a product of the society of neo yo  Kyo and it isn't easy to overcome social  conditioning and see outside the box if  that box is all you've ever known if  Kass could change so easily  and suddenly become a better person then  the social commentary would be far less  potent if it were so easy to escape the  shackles of conformity that modern  society places upon us then anyone could  do it but it isn't easy and that's the  point  after all in real life many people never  quote-unquote develop at all they remain  greedy vain and pretentious for their  entire lives whoever in no yoki oh we do  have helymus and Tesoro and she is a  character who sees outside the box a  former fashion blogger who built a Jake  Paul er esque following through her  online fashion blogging she comes to see  the absurdity of modern society and  rebels against it by rejecting  fashionable clothing and the meaningless  social spectacles of neo ukyo's high  society through Helena we get to  experience the full extent of Neal  ukyo's absurdity and because of her our  protagonist Kaz begins to reevaluate  some of his priorities if ever so  slightly when he eventually decides to  help her and of course we also have the  famous big Toblerone which can be said  to have important symbolic meaning as  well one could argue that the big  Toblerone represents the strong desire  for social acceptance that so many of  the characters in neo yoyo express and  the Toblerone is therefore a symbol of  conformity if you conform to society's  expectations then you deserve a big  Toblerone but if you don't then no  Toblerone for you finally cast a  protagonist may not be a simplistic of a  character as we think he could be looked  at as the Millennial Hamlet an  indecisive melancholic self-hating  existentialist madman but he is not to  blame for this not entirely because he  is the product of his society and is the  Society of neo yoki oh really that  different from our society  that is the question that we are left  with and it is an interesting one all  things considered and regardless of  whether you like me or yo kyo for its  humor or its underlying themes or  whether you just hate everything about  it I think that it's a great thing that  neo yo Kyo exists it's very existence  proves that anime is becoming globally  recognized to the point that an entire  Netflix series with a star-studded cast  would pay tribute to anime in such a  direct way as long as we don't expect it  to be something that it's not as long as  we don't compare it to high quality  anime and just enjoy it for the  satirical and surreal anime inspired  American comedy that it is there will be  plenty of big Toblerone z' to go around  for everyone now if you enjoyed this  video be sure to leave a like in order  to help me move up in the most eligible  bachelor rankings and if you're new to  the channel don't forget to subscribe  and hit that notification bell as always  thank you so much for watching and until  next time see us space Cowboys  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you  [Music]

